Why: READ_BENCH (used only when KEEP(403) /= 0) reads a benchmark file
 named relative to the working directory into BENCH, which has a single
 element, so upstream writes out of bounds whenever the file exists. The
 routine now zeroes BENCH and returns. T1 removes its file I/O
 (IO-Disabled in tools/manifest/mumps.dcf).
Upstream: not sent; worth reporting (out-of-bounds BENCH).
Obsolete when: upstream sizes BENCH or removes READ_BENCH.

--- a/src/ana_omp_m.F
+++ b/src/ana_omp_m.F
@@ -862,6 +862,10 @@
       PARAMETER(NLINES=2812)
       DOUBLE PRECISION :: AUX
       CHARACTER(1)             :: K50_STR
+C     rmumps: benchmark files are not read (the file name is relative to
+C     the working directory, and BENCH has a single element anyway).
+      BENCH = 0.0D0
+      RETURN
       INDEX_NPIV = 0
       INDEX_NSCHUR = 0
       OLD_V = -1
